# Exclusions for `trivy config` scans over this repository.
# Format: one Trivy check id per line. Blank / `#`-prefixed lines are
# ignored. Every entry MUST have a rationale immediately above it.

# DS-0002 — "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root
# user as argument".
#
# This image intentionally boots as root. The entrypoint script needs
# root to:
#   - reconcile the `asterisk` user's uid/gid with the runtime-provided
#     PUID / PGID (Unraid volumes typically want 99:100),
#   - chown the bind-mounted directories (/etc/asterisk, /var/log/asterisk,
#     /var/lib/asterisk/{db,keys,sounds}, /var/spool/asterisk) so that
#     Asterisk can write to them,
#   - render `*.conf.template` files via envsubst.
#
# Once that is done, Asterisk itself drops privileges via `-U asterisk -p`
# in CMD, so the long-running process does *not* run as root. Adding
# `USER asterisk` at the Dockerfile level would break the entrypoint's
# chown step and force users to pre-chown their volumes on the host
# (which defeats the point of PUID/PGID).
DS-0002
